WEBVTT

00:04.530 --> 00:07.110
I was physically abused by my father.

00:09.280 --> 00:11.490
Do you remember when it started?

00:12.120 --> 00:16.580
The first time he took me to that
atelier was when I was around four.

00:17.040 --> 00:18.750
And it continued after that?

00:19.330 --> 00:20.290
Yes.

00:21.750 --> 00:22.840
On that day too?

00:23.630 --> 00:24.670
Yes.

00:25.380 --> 00:29.180
On that day too, my father called me as usual.

00:29.180 --> 00:31.390
He would say, "It's art time".

00:31.890 --> 00:33.180
Then...

00:42.060 --> 00:43.610
So, you're finally done?

00:44.230 --> 00:47.740
The questioning alone took half a month.

00:47.740 --> 00:50.910
I'm sorry. You guys have been accompanying me all this time.

00:50.910 --> 00:53.620
Oh, no. That's not what I meant.

00:53.620 --> 00:55.120
My father requested me to as well.

00:55.620 --> 00:57.660
I'm free anyway.

00:58.870 --> 01:01.960
Say, Fumika. Why did you press charges?

01:01.960 --> 01:03.210
Hey, don't, Natsuka.

01:04.130 --> 01:08.720
I won't be able to move forward if I don't
settle the problem with my father by myself.

01:09.380 --> 01:11.550
You sure have changed, Fumika.

01:12.140 --> 01:13.640
I have to change.

01:14.140 --> 01:14.800
No...

01:16.220 --> 01:17.060
I will change.

01:20.810 --> 01:22.650
The true forms

01:22.400 --> 01:22.650
Of the things that I gazed at

01:24.230 --> 01:24.480
Were for showing after I closed my eyes

01:25.320 --> 01:28.190
Shigofumi

01:27.940 --> 01:28.190
Again today, time

01:29.820 --> 01:30.070
Will only construct a loneliness

01:31.610 --> 01:31.860
That seems to be torn apart, right?

01:39.040 --> 01:39.290
There are people who can't forget about

01:42.710 --> 01:42.960
The white lotuses that bloom in the darkness

01:46.340 --> 01:46.590
Nevertheless, recollections

01:50.090 --> 01:50.340
Visit from the future

01:53.760 --> 01:54.010
Words that turn into sighs

02:01.140 --> 02:01.390
Are the emerging wings of the soul

02:04.850 --> 02:05.100
Will I flutter apart?

02:08.570 --> 02:08.820
Growing confused and disordered

02:12.240 --> 02:12.490
I want to carve

02:14.530 --> 02:14.780
These letters to you

02:19.580 --> 02:19.830
Pieces of the truth

02:21.410 --> 02:21.660
Of things that I want to tell you-

02:23.290 --> 02:23.540
I can't even send them well to you

02:27.000 --> 02:27.250
If I write them with the blood that stains my fingertips

02:30.670 --> 02:30.920
Then can they spill into your heart?

02:34.380 --> 02:34.630
Even if the one word left behind

02:37.600 --> 02:37.850
To us who live

02:40.310 --> 02:40.560
Is to be goodbye

02:49.980 --> 02:52.320
Mikawa Fumika

02:50.860 --> 02:52.320
Go ahead, Fumika-san.

02:53.280 --> 02:57.030
I'm Mikawa Fumika. Nice to meet you all.

03:14.920 --> 03:15.880
It's here!

03:15.880 --> 03:17.090
Hurry!

03:20.350 --> 03:21.890
She's a real beauty.

03:21.890 --> 03:22.350
Really?

03:23.140 --> 03:24.270
What's that about?

03:24.270 --> 03:26.190
Mikawa Kirameki's daughter, right?

03:27.770 --> 03:29.110
There are phone messages circulating.

03:29.730 --> 03:31.570
It's being spread on the Net as well.

03:32.070 --> 03:33.860
About her being abused or whatever.

03:36.280 --> 03:38.450
Senpai asked to send a follow-up report.

03:38.450 --> 03:39.450
He must like her.

03:56.630 --> 03:57.720
Mikawa.

04:01.510 --> 04:02.850
Kaname-kun.

04:02.850 --> 04:03.850
What's up?

04:03.850 --> 04:05.020
Nothing much.

04:05.390 --> 04:07.600
Just been a while since I've chatted with you at school.

04:07.600 --> 04:09.690
This is the first time you've been in high school, right?

04:09.980 --> 04:11.560
I was wondering what you thought of it.

04:14.440 --> 04:15.860
It's fun.

04:16.400 --> 04:17.950
I'm glad I came after all.

04:22.330 --> 04:25.750
I'm going to submit an application to the
Gospel Department to get a replacement.

04:26.250 --> 04:27.710
I'm sorry.

04:31.580 --> 04:33.670
What did you do this time?

04:33.670 --> 04:35.710
I got the confirmation code wrong.

04:35.710 --> 04:37.420
And I burned my partner...

04:38.630 --> 04:40.130
Ah, so that's why.

04:40.510 --> 04:43.430
My partner however, seems burnt out.

04:43.430 --> 04:44.220
Chiaki?

04:44.680 --> 04:48.730
Just when she found a law that'd
be able to get Fumika acknowledged...

04:49.310 --> 04:52.520
the Fumika in question vanished.

04:57.820 --> 04:59.900
Today, we'll resume where we left off yesterday.

04:59.900 --> 05:04.240
We will be discussing the popular novelist,
Mikawa Kirameki's, child abuse case.

05:05.080 --> 05:07.080
Mikawa Kirameki sued by daughter

05:05.080 --> 05:07.080
Movie Version!!

05:05.700 --> 05:09.040
It has been a week since his daughter filed charges.

05:09.330 --> 05:13.670
But, the scars must have been deep to force
her to file charges against her own father.

05:14.380 --> 05:17.210
But, that's no reason to point a gun at your own father.

05:17.840 --> 05:21.010
No matter what the reason, he's still her father.

05:21.680 --> 05:23.640
And furthermore...

05:23.640 --> 05:29.390
I feel the way this information was leaked
out is even more of a problem.

05:29.930 --> 05:33.520
I guess this is what you call the collapse
of morals in modern society.

05:37.020 --> 05:37.110
Mikawa Kirameki disappears before
book launching!?

05:37.020 --> 05:37.110
Request
to tone
down
over-
heated
reporting

05:37.020 --> 05:37.110
Abusive father punished by daughter

05:38.940 --> 05:40.490
Please give us a few words.

05:40.490 --> 05:41.150
A few words.

05:41.150 --> 05:41.990
Please.

05:42.320 --> 05:43.780
How's his daughter's condition?

05:43.780 --> 05:46.030
Your comments on why Mikawa Kirameki is hiding, please.

05:46.030 --> 05:47.540
Please.

05:54.540 --> 05:58.170
Yes. I booked the room under the director's name.

05:58.750 --> 06:00.720
Kirameki-sensei is already in the room.

06:00.720 --> 06:04.300
We're considering countermeasures at the moment.

06:04.300 --> 06:05.050
<i>Counter?</i>

06:05.510 --> 06:07.050
I mean it literally.

06:07.640 --> 06:10.600
A bestselling author whom the whole world is against.

06:10.600 --> 06:12.310
It'll be difficult to balance.

06:12.850 --> 06:15.610
It looks like we won't be able to do it like we did before.

06:15.940 --> 06:18.070
Be on standby over there.

06:19.730 --> 06:20.530
Yes sir.

06:23.740 --> 06:25.660
Where should we go now?

06:26.120 --> 06:29.990
Sorry for always making you wait in front of our school.

06:29.990 --> 06:31.160
It's okay...

06:32.540 --> 06:34.540
Fumika sure is late.

06:34.540 --> 06:35.460
Yeah.

06:37.080 --> 06:40.000
Why don't you say anything?

06:40.000 --> 06:40.960
About?

06:40.960 --> 06:42.340
About Mika.

06:44.550 --> 06:47.550
Probably for the same reasons as you.

06:49.430 --> 06:51.600
We have no choice but to accept it, right?

07:10.700 --> 07:12.370
Kaname-kun...

07:12.830 --> 07:15.620
the one you fell in love with was Mika, right?

07:15.620 --> 07:16.460
Huh?

07:16.460 --> 07:17.540
How did you...?

07:18.000 --> 07:20.210
I know at least that much.

07:22.300 --> 07:24.590
Is that why you're so nice to Fumika?

07:25.090 --> 07:27.090
Because Mika is inside her?

07:27.090 --> 07:28.390
That's unrelated!

07:28.390 --> 07:29.390
It <i>is</i> related!

07:30.720 --> 07:31.850
Natsuka.

07:34.480 --> 07:35.640
Because...

07:36.140 --> 07:38.190
I love you.

07:39.270 --> 07:42.270
Nojima Kaname-kun, I love you.

07:55.830 --> 07:58.460
Why did you go home without us today?

07:59.420 --> 08:00.500
Sorry.

08:07.880 --> 08:10.800
Say, back then at the shrine...

08:13.100 --> 08:16.480
I thought I heard a gunshot.

08:16.480 --> 08:17.980
Was it just my imagination?

08:23.360 --> 08:25.480
Yes, it was.

08:26.900 --> 08:27.900
Night.

08:31.450 --> 08:32.780
Mika...

08:34.080 --> 08:34.950
I mustn't.

08:35.750 --> 08:39.040
This time, I shall do it on my own.

08:39.580 --> 08:41.210
With my own strength.

08:43.630 --> 08:45.710
The police already made a request to them.

08:45.710 --> 08:49.430
From now on, the journalists will control themselves.

08:49.430 --> 08:52.220
That's why so many came today.

08:52.220 --> 08:54.010
So many cameras and mics.

08:54.010 --> 08:55.930
They'll surely come again tomorrow.

08:55.930 --> 08:56.810
Come on.

08:56.810 --> 08:59.350
It's because you aren't here in the afternoons.

08:59.350 --> 09:02.730
I'm worried that they'll take
pictures or try interview Natsuka.

09:10.400 --> 09:11.410
Work?

09:11.410 --> 09:12.530
No.

09:12.530 --> 09:14.080
Then, what is it?

09:14.990 --> 09:18.330
Partners are obligated to move together.

09:20.290 --> 09:22.080
Do as you please.

09:28.840 --> 09:30.510
Buongiorno.

09:32.300 --> 09:36.100
Where in Italy did she say she was living again?

09:36.100 --> 09:37.810
Oh, sorry.

09:37.810 --> 09:39.850
I'm bad at remembering Katakana words.

09:39.850 --> 09:42.810
Not at all. I'll ask her myself when I see her.

09:49.860 --> 09:51.150
Buongiorno!

09:54.740 --> 09:56.160
Nice to meet you.

09:57.540 --> 09:58.830
Mum.

09:59.120 --> 10:01.120
Shigofumi

10:02.250 --> 10:04.250
Shigofumi

10:04.920 --> 10:06.880
Aizawa Kirei-san.

10:07.210 --> 10:10.460
I'm Nojima of the Kamome Police Department.

10:10.460 --> 10:13.260
Ah, you're the detective. Thank you for the phone call.

10:28.940 --> 10:30.730
You sure have grown up.

10:30.730 --> 10:32.780
And you've become really beautiful as well.

10:34.860 --> 10:37.620
I guess it's only natural since you're his and my child.

10:37.620 --> 10:39.950
You will become more beautiful.

10:41.580 --> 10:43.460
Beauty is strength.

10:43.460 --> 10:45.330
Please become strong.

10:45.330 --> 10:47.960
My daughter would be able to do this, right?

10:47.960 --> 10:48.670
Huh?

10:49.840 --> 10:52.010
So, with that...

10:52.840 --> 10:55.090
Detective, I'll be going now.

10:55.090 --> 10:55.430
Eh?

10:55.840 --> 10:58.640
What do you mean you're leaving?

10:58.640 --> 11:02.810
It's because I still want to be a woman.

11:02.810 --> 11:03.730
Huh?

11:04.020 --> 11:06.350
I don't wish to be a mother.

11:06.350 --> 11:08.360
I'll pay for her living expenses.

11:08.360 --> 11:10.110
What are you saying?

11:10.110 --> 11:12.320
It's exactly as I mentioned on the phone.

11:12.320 --> 11:14.030
She no longer has...

11:14.320 --> 11:17.820
I'm not fit to be a mother.

11:18.280 --> 11:19.450
Then...

11:19.990 --> 11:22.160
Then, why did you give birth to me?

11:22.160 --> 11:23.910
And why did you marry Daddy too?

11:26.420 --> 11:31.590
Because I wanted to taste the joys of womanhood at least once.

11:32.130 --> 11:37.130
Engagement ring, wedding
ceremony, honeymoon, childbirth, I guess.

11:38.050 --> 11:40.640
I don't mind having another wedding.

11:40.640 --> 11:42.970
But, childbirth is different.

11:44.270 --> 11:45.680
Kirei-san!

11:45.680 --> 11:46.810
Lorenzo!

11:46.810 --> 11:47.390
Loren-

11:47.390 --> 11:48.940
See you, Fumika.

11:48.940 --> 11:52.150
Lorenzo said that he wanted to see Kyoto.

11:52.690 --> 11:53.570
Mum!

11:53.570 --> 11:55.110
Oh my little kitty cat.

11:55.110 --> 11:57.530
Oh my cute little piggy.

12:06.040 --> 12:07.370
Fumika-chan...

12:27.350 --> 12:28.730
Isn't that Aizawa Kirei?

12:28.730 --> 12:29.690
Her daughter is here.

12:29.690 --> 12:31.360
The one who pressed charges.

12:31.360 --> 12:32.610
It's her?

12:32.610 --> 12:34.320
Fumika-chan, what's wrong?

12:34.780 --> 12:35.730
Fumika-chan.

12:37.700 --> 12:38.700
Fumika-chan!

12:41.410 --> 12:42.620
Fumika-chan!

12:43.410 --> 12:45.370
Kasai
Natsuka

12:43.410 --> 12:45.370
Make
call?

12:43.410 --> 12:45.370
Voice
call

12:43.410 --> 12:45.370
Video
call

12:43.410 --> 12:45.370
Group
talk

12:46.040 --> 12:48.040
She told me out of the blue.

12:48.040 --> 12:49.500
I don't know how to answer.

12:51.170 --> 12:53.790
I don't think there are many places she can go.

12:54.250 --> 12:56.420
I'll continue searching this area.

12:56.710 --> 13:00.260
Okay. I'll try searching some places I have in mind.

13:00.260 --> 13:02.390
Sorry. I'm counting on you.

13:08.810 --> 13:11.770
We're not going to hide Kirameki any longer.

13:12.310 --> 13:13.860
This horse is simply too large.

13:14.230 --> 13:16.230
What will become of his book?

13:17.440 --> 13:21.410
Kirameki-sensei certainly should be punished for his crimes.

13:21.860 --> 13:23.490
But, his work...

13:24.580 --> 13:27.660
There should be no crime in the words he wrote.

13:27.660 --> 13:29.960
You're planning to release a book by a criminal?

13:29.960 --> 13:30.540
Yes.

13:30.540 --> 13:31.210
Whoa there...

13:31.750 --> 13:35.340
We've become successful because of him.

13:35.340 --> 13:39.550
Aren't we already accomplices since we were paid?

13:39.550 --> 13:40.630
Kasai-san.

13:45.180 --> 13:47.560
My sister is currently in a meeting.

13:47.560 --> 13:49.980
I heard from my mother as well.

13:49.980 --> 13:51.560
I see.

13:52.060 --> 13:55.190
That would mean, she must be at Kirameki's house.

13:55.690 --> 13:56.610
Thanks.

13:56.610 --> 13:57.610
Wait.

14:00.360 --> 14:03.990
The Fumika you fell in love with is gone.

14:04.620 --> 14:05.740
What's this, all of a sudden?

14:06.330 --> 14:08.620
The present Fumika isn't Mika.

14:08.620 --> 14:09.790
She's Fumi.

14:09.790 --> 14:11.830
That's unrelated.

14:12.330 --> 14:14.250
But, she shot her!

14:14.750 --> 14:16.290
She shot Mika.

14:26.390 --> 14:28.140
I'm such an idiot.

14:28.140 --> 14:30.310
I detested this place, yet...

14:50.200 --> 14:51.580
In the end...

15:04.510 --> 15:05.300
Mika?

15:11.520 --> 15:13.560
W-Why?

15:13.850 --> 15:16.020
Don't come near me!

15:16.480 --> 15:19.360
I am your fragility, because you're naive.

15:19.360 --> 15:20.980
Don't come near me!

15:20.980 --> 15:22.730
You haven't changed at all.

15:23.150 --> 15:25.320
You have to fire the gun yourself.

15:47.760 --> 15:50.050
You have to try on your own from now on.

16:01.110 --> 16:03.530
Right after I set my mind to it...

16:04.190 --> 16:06.150
you tell me to try on my own.

16:06.150 --> 16:07.860
You tell me that I have to try my best.

16:08.530 --> 16:11.200
In spite of that, why...?

16:12.700 --> 16:14.870
Why did you appear again?!

16:16.580 --> 16:18.790
Because you were planning on running away again.

16:18.790 --> 16:19.500
Don't lie!

16:19.790 --> 16:21.750
You ran from Kaname, Natsuka, and the rest.

16:21.750 --> 16:24.130
You ran from your problems with Mother.

16:24.130 --> 16:25.550
And also now.

16:25.550 --> 16:28.050
I didn't run!

16:33.890 --> 16:37.680
People from the world outside don't swing such weak blows.

16:40.770 --> 16:43.400
I know that!

16:44.190 --> 16:45.940
It's your fault, Mika!

16:46.530 --> 16:49.320
You always snatch away the things I try to do.

16:51.240 --> 16:54.950
Mika's gone because she shot her with the gun, right?

16:56.200 --> 16:58.250
I can't smile about something like that.

16:59.540 --> 17:01.750
Her suffering...

17:01.750 --> 17:03.750
is the consequence of her own doing.

17:06.380 --> 17:07.970
I'm going though.

17:09.170 --> 17:11.390
Love or hate...

17:11.890 --> 17:13.760
it's not about that any more.

17:29.700 --> 17:31.110
Give it up.

17:31.110 --> 17:32.910
You won't be able to beat me.

17:38.290 --> 17:41.370
Why? Why didn't you wait?

17:42.080 --> 17:43.880
Until I had gathered enough courage.

17:43.880 --> 17:45.840
Until I was able to give it a go.

17:49.630 --> 17:51.260
You can be the one to shoot.

17:51.550 --> 17:53.090
You want to disappear, don't you?

17:53.090 --> 17:56.810
But, you came out because I was so pathetic, right?

17:56.810 --> 17:58.140
Then, the answer is simple!

17:58.520 --> 18:01.350
Shoot me and both of us will disappear.

18:03.520 --> 18:05.690
You'll be able to shoot, right?

18:06.190 --> 18:07.440
Shoot me!

18:09.530 --> 18:10.490
I...

18:13.110 --> 18:14.660
You were doing it for me?

18:14.660 --> 18:17.620
You were the one who wanted friends, weren't you?

18:17.620 --> 18:19.160
You liar!

18:19.450 --> 18:22.120
You want to live too!

18:22.460 --> 18:24.080
You don't want to disappear!

18:34.800 --> 18:37.010
Not about that any more?

18:37.550 --> 18:39.220
Then what is it about?

18:40.680 --> 18:42.310
Fumika doesn't even exist.

18:42.310 --> 18:42.930
She does.

18:42.930 --> 18:43.350
Huh?

18:43.690 --> 18:44.520
Kanaka?

18:44.520 --> 18:47.770
It's really careless leaving the veranda upstairs unlocked.

18:47.770 --> 18:50.150
But, that's not important.

18:51.860 --> 18:53.320
Fumika exists.

18:53.320 --> 18:56.370
She was with me all this while for three years.

18:56.370 --> 18:58.950
I've been thinking since that time.

18:58.950 --> 19:01.580
I don't really understand human illnesses.

19:01.580 --> 19:03.870
But, Fumika was definitely with me.

19:03.870 --> 19:05.870
She was my partner.

19:05.870 --> 19:08.500
Don't say something as shameful like, "She doesn't exist".

19:08.960 --> 19:11.380
I can tell you for sure that Fumika exists.

19:11.380 --> 19:14.050
Don't try to make it as if she doesn't.

19:14.880 --> 19:16.390
Ah! Slow down!

19:16.720 --> 19:19.510
I'm going to hit the floor!

19:19.510 --> 19:21.600
We're in a hurry so bear with it.

19:23.020 --> 19:24.520
I remember.

19:25.020 --> 19:27.560
Obviously I remember.

19:27.560 --> 19:30.520
I love both Fumikas.

19:35.110 --> 19:36.240
That's right!

19:37.320 --> 19:39.700
I wanted to make friends too.

19:39.700 --> 19:41.240
I wanted to try basketball too.

19:41.240 --> 19:44.160
Family too, school too, even work.

19:44.620 --> 19:47.040
I wanted to wear the uniform
and go to school every morning.

19:47.040 --> 19:48.170
I wanted to make box lunches.

19:48.170 --> 19:50.790
I wanted to go with friends to karaoke too!

19:50.790 --> 19:51.750
Sukiyaki!

19:52.050 --> 19:53.000
A date with my boyfriend.

19:53.300 --> 19:54.130
Exchanging e-mails!

19:54.130 --> 19:55.170
Culture festival!

19:55.170 --> 19:57.180
Cooking yakisoba wearing an apron!

19:57.180 --> 19:59.590
Create a play, act in it, celebrate!

20:18.280 --> 20:20.660
It's a future that may have actually come true.

20:21.740 --> 20:23.330
It's the same with the Shigofumi.

20:24.370 --> 20:25.790
What do you mean?

20:26.910 --> 20:29.500
Rightfully, this mail should not have been sendable.

20:34.800 --> 20:37.050
I failed to tell you something very important.

20:37.920 --> 20:40.720
I was a personality that never existed before.

20:41.260 --> 20:44.180
That's why I thought it was only right that I disappeared.

20:46.890 --> 20:48.940
Thank you for bringing me out.

21:04.790 --> 21:06.160
I hate you!

21:06.660 --> 21:09.000
I hate you, Mika!

21:12.790 --> 21:16.420
I hate you!

21:26.930 --> 21:28.100
Fumika!

21:29.730 --> 21:32.060
Eh? What's going on?

21:32.060 --> 21:33.150
No idea.

21:34.020 --> 21:35.570
They both exist, right?

21:36.150 --> 21:38.110
Isn't that good enough?

21:47.790 --> 21:50.460
Yep, it is.

21:51.290 --> 21:56.130
Shigofumi

21:51.290 --> 21:56.130
Episode Twelve

23:04.530 --> 23:06.740
I'm not going to
switch places with you.

23:07.320 --> 23:11.490
I'm never going to let
you back inside me, Mika.

23:17.880 --> 23:20.300
Kanaka, 0609.

23:27.800 --> 23:28.850
People's good will.

23:29.760 --> 23:31.220
